Id: lin047i
Severity: INFO
Category: kernel
Check: check_sysctl
Fix: Set net.core.bpf_jit_harden=2 in /etc/sysctl.d.
References: Linux kernel sysctl documentation (admin-guide/sysctl/net, bpf_jit_harden); sysctl.d(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 10.5; NIST CM-6, SI-16; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

net.core.bpf_jit_harden is below 2: the BPF JIT compiler writes the
constants of a program into executable kernel memory as they are.
With hardening on they are blinded (each replaced by a random value
and the operation that restores it), so a program cannot plant chosen
bytes to jump into later, which is what JIT spraying does. 1 hardens
the programs of users without CAP_BPF or CAP_SYS_ADMIN, 2 everyone's,
at some cost in speed. The kernel's default is 0 and no distribution
changes it; where unprivileged BPF is off already (lin025w) only 2
adds anything, against a root-level process that has gone bad. A
hardening opportunity: Lynis asks for 2, the CIS Benchmarks do not
name the key.
  # sysctl -w net.core.bpf_jit_harden=2
